WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
Three white powders sit
on the bench: glucose,

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.550
starch and a protein.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.070
They look exactly the same,

4
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.190
and in a lab you never taste anything.

5
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.450
But add a few drops of
the right chemical,

6
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.370
and each one gives itself
away with a colour change.

7
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.750
So what colour would each one turn?

8
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.130
In this mission, you'll test
for starch with iodine,

9
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.810
for sugars with Benedict's solution,

10
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.170
and for protein with biuret.

11
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.610
You'll learn how to
carry out each test,

12
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.870
and how to read the result.

13
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.570
And you'll meet a test for fats too.

14
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.550
Your mission: work out how to
tell the three powders apart.
